            {
              "task": "killing-all-sessions-wipes-restore-state-4-2",
              "source": "reviewer",
              "summary": "A session name containing the listing's field separator blocks every save for as long as that session exists, and breaks every session-list reader.",
              "failure": "A user who renames a session to `work|notes` in the picker (ValidateSessionName accepts it) or creates it with tmux directly gets no committed save from the tick, the shutdown flush or commit-now until that session is gone; saved state goes stale so a reboot restores an old snapshot, and ListSessions errors for the whole listing so the picker, completion, portal list and restore's live-set read lose the other sessions too; the only sign is a repeating tick failed WARN / commit cycle failed ERROR in portal.log. The pane captureFormat separator `|||` has the same exposure for a name containing `|||`.",
              "detail": "listSessionsArgs / parseSessionList SplitN(line, \"|\", 4) (internal/tmux/tmux.go:147,190). @portal-dir can only take the trailing slot, so the name cannot also go last. Options: a separator tmux names cannot carry (a control character), or ValidateSessionName plus SanitiseProjectName refusing `|`. Rename modal check at internal/tui/model.go:2869, RenameSession's at internal/tmux/tmux.go:323. Refusing in the validator does not cover sessions created outside Portal, so the format change is the complete fix.",
              "files": [
                "internal/tmux/tmux.go",
                "internal/tmux/errors.go",
                "internal/session/naming.go",
                "internal/state/capture.go",
                "internal/tui/model.go"
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      }
